From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:17:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 66/70] hottyterm: what plays out of view asks for no frames

A hotty surface whose placement was scrolled out of the view, or whose
window was hidden (minimised, covered), kept asking for a frame of every
CSS animation on it, and each frame was painted, uploaded and drawn at the
display's rate for pixels nobody saw. The terminal now tells hotty-blitz
which surfaces can be seen (hotty_host_set_seen): placed on the screen
that shows, on rows of the view, in a window that is visible. It looks
again whenever it schedules a frame, when the renderer finds that the view
moved (a scroll, output pushing lines up), and when the window is hidden
or shown. Seen again, a surface asks for a frame at once, at the time it
then is.

Adds 8 lines in upstream files: a hook in the renderer's frame, the
renderer state's pointer to the surfaces, and one in the occlusion
callback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
